  <revision rev="6" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>714f5dab298ea8da29d6095bc3088d65</srcmd5>
    <version>9.8.2</version>
    <time>1786737895</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 9.8.2

Upstream 9.8.2. One user-visible fix: the reader code no longer writes to
stdout, which was polluting zimcheck's output. The tag also carries a
deduplication of the Xapian stemmer initialisation and a move to
zim-testing-suite 0.10.0 for upstream's own CI.

That test-suite bump does not affect this package: the spec builds with
-Dtest_data_dir=none, so the external test data is never fetched and
zim-testing-suite is not a dependency here. The 31 tests that do run are all
green.

SONAME is unchanged -- meson project version 9.8.2, major still 9 -- so
libzim9 keeps its name and no reverse dependency needs rebuilding.

Worth noting for anyone checking this against a release feed: upstream tagged
9.8.2 without attaching a GitHub release object, so release-based trackers
still report 9.8.1 as newest. The tag is a deliberate release commit (a
release_9.8.2 pull request with its own ChangeLog entry) and the archive URL
this package already uses resolves normally, so there is no missing-source
risk.

Verified on aarch64: build green, 31 tests pass with 0 failures, rpmlint
0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370917</requestid>
  </revision>
